# Act configuration for the rig.
#
# Everything runs on the host — the rig IS the CI runner. All runner labels
# (including the GPU labels [self-hosted, cuda, rtx3060]) are mapped to Act's
# host-runner pseudo-image `-self-hosted` so Act executes the job steps directly
# in the devenv shell that launched `act` (no containers: the CUDA toolkit, the
# GPUs, the model cache, and the nix libcuda-first LD_LIBRARY_PATH are all
# host-local). The workflow steps source ci/runner/rig-env.sh for the rig facts
# (model paths, CCACHE_DIR, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, NIXPKGS_ALLOW_UNFREE, GPU 0 pin).
#
# Run from the repo root inside the devenv shell:
#   NIXPKGS_ALLOW_UNFREE=1 devenv shell -- act -l
--workflows=ci/workflows
-P ubuntu-latest=-self-hosted
-P self-hosted=-self-hosted
-P cuda=-self-hosted
-P rtx3060=-self-hosted
-P cpu=-self-hosted
